(:id "port/luau/packet" :state :done :evidence ("internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireReadsTheGoldens" "internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireReadNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luau/write_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireWritesTheGoldens" "internal/codegen/luau/write_test.go: TestLuauTypeWireWriteNegativeControl" "internal/codegen/luau/read_test.go: TestLuauSelectedArmStartsAtItsDefaults" "internal/codegen/luau/serialize_vendor_test.go: TestVendoredLuauSerializeIsThePin" "make packet-utf8-luau, packet-utf8-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-wide-luau, packet-wide-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-defaults-luau, packet-defaults-luau-negative-control (make/luau-packet.mk)" "make packet-finite-luau, packet-finite-luau-negative-control (make/luau.mk)" "make schema-luau-generated-analyze-strict-gate, schema-luau-generated-analyze-strict-gate-negative-control") :tested-revision "2f56f1130ea5c4bf3a4152fec1ca66349081be6d" :note "2026-11-04: The Luau packet leg (internal/codegen/luau, the vendored serialize.luau) reads and writes every shared packet golden byte-identical to C++, with a read and a write negative control that go red. The four packet gates pass on the pin with their controls: packet-text (33 pinned rows and 496 bit flips agree with C++, 192 mutated refusals), packet-wide (32 pinned rows and 1016 bit flips agree with C++, 503 mutated refusals), packet-defaults and packet-finite. The generated code passes luau-analyze --mode=strict, and its planted-pattern control goes red. Run on hetzner1 (Linux x86-64) at main 2f56f1130 under Luau 0.741 (make dist-luau), SCHEMA_SLOW=1.")
